{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":27,"timestamp":"2026-06-15T18:17:08.992676496Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a1fcfbb8-6b7e-443c-975b-cefaf76c7d1f","title":"as_strided accepts negative strides that torch rejects","description":"Live PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130 rejects torch.as_strided(x, (3,), (-1,), 1) with RuntimeError: negative strides are not supported. ferrotorch-core currently has an as_strided_negative_stride_reverses unit test and accepts the CPU case while CUDA strided-copy rejects negative strides, creating CPU/CUDA and PyTorch divergence. This was discovered while auditing CORE-004/#1698 and is intentionally tracked separately from the OOB-safety fix. Acceptance: public as_strided/as_strided_copy/as_strided_scatter semantics match torch for negative strides across CPU/CUDA, with regression tests proving the structured error and no invalid view metadata escape.","priority":"medium","created_by":"y4rr"},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMB3uJbiqsdxEkt4Nz7G7mOACy1SMFTNG1XHFPG71I/MCXnn7cbX/L+a0oChukROrJfU6DEmUvUKyd38+AKIyAE="}
